      "content": "Start by gathering all transaction details for the specific accounts over the past three months to identify if these irregularities cluster around specific individuals, vendors, or timeframes. You can then cross-reference these transactions with digital payment logs or vendor contracts to spot inconsistencies without needing formal forensics. If the root cause is found to be genuine exceptions or minor errors, adjust the internal controls accordingly; if fraud is suspected, escalate the findings immediately for a formal audit. This proactive approach addresses the issue efficiently while maintaining transparency.",
